{
  "__doc": "Each block's composition role (section-root | wrapper-shell | content-block | leaf), the block it wraps and its container kind. THE source of truth for the seeded columns of the `block_composition` table. dbschema/seed_reference_data.py seeds it from this file (rows the file lacks are deleted).",
  "__why": "composition_role has no derive-from-code populator, and a rebuild-from-empty produced only 39 of these 226 rows (the other 187 lived only in the shared database), which broke every skeleton proposal that reads a block's role. This file also carries what seed-composition-roles.py used to apply (its role corrections and the rows it added for later blocks); that script is deleted. Edit THIS file to change a role or add a block.",
  "__not_captured": "accepts_allowed_blocks: sgs-update-v2.py derives it from edit.js (the Stage 1 allowedBlocks scrape); the seeder never writes it. A core block's row names a block whose `blocks` row exists only after a stage 2 scrape: the seeder writes it anyway (foreign keys are off for the seed).",
  "__columns": [
    "block_slug",
    "wraps_block",
    "composition_role",
    "container_kind"
  ],
